<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Barca</h1><p class="st-meta">560 BCE – 322 BCE (approx.) · capital Barca</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Greek city of Cyrenaica founded by rebel Battiad princes, remembered for its brutal destruction by the Persians.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> relates that around 560 BCE the brothers of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcesilaus-ii">Arcesilaus II</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-cyrene">Kingdom of Cyrene</a> quarrelled with him and founded Barca, on the plain inland from the coast (near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-marj">al-Marj</a>), with the support of local <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/libu">Libyans</a>. The city soon became a rival of its mother city.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Barca was a Greek city of mixed Greek and Libyan population, ruled at first by kings; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> names a king Alazeir, whose daughter married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcesilaus-iii">Arcesilaus III of Cyrene</a>. It was known for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horse-breeding">horse breeding</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariots</a>. When Arcesilaus III was murdered there, his mother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pheretime">Pheretime</a> called in the Persian governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aryandes">Aryandes</a>, whose army took Barca around 515 BCE by trickery after a long siege.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Many Barcaeans were deported to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/greco-bactrian-kingdom">Bactria</a>. The city recovered as a member of the Cyrenaican cities, but declined as its port, Ptolemais, grew. It passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ptolemaic-empire">Ptolemaic Empire</a> in 322 BCE.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 560 BCE – 322 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:48.56%;width:4.74%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>560 BCE – 322 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Barca</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Alazeir</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ancient Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/libya">Libya</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Barce, Ptolemais</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-441&amp;focus=barca" aria-label="Barca on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5216 996 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Barca lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5536 1252L5560 1241M5536 1252L6140 1251M5536 1252L5772 1297"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5560 1241h0M6140 1251h0M5772 1297h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5536 1252h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5536 1252h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Barca. <a href="/atlas?year=-441&amp;focus=barca">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
